     oracle nuisances give an exact SE and nominal coverage; the shipped estimator's
     excess variance is fold-split noise (.corner_fit redraws folds per call), and
     reps>1 (already shipped) brings the POINT estimate to oracle efficiency for
     continuous Y, but coverage stays ~0.88 because the SE estimator itself has
     CV 0.5-0.8 across datasets (oracle 0.17); (2) near-null cells — even the
     oracle SE explodes (se/sd 591, 333): the ratio is non-regular, exactly A1's
     regime. Binary tau=0 n=800 is a transition cell (dataset-level
     near-singularity; reps=10 halves but does not finish). ONE well-posed open
     problem: an SE estimator for the reps>1 point estimator (candidates ranked in
     FINDINGS §Open) — RESOLVED later the same day, see FINDINGS §Open item 1:
     full-sample-nuisance IF variance; not yet shipped. Also delivered in PR #33: the A2/Zhan attribution fix in
     R/gauge-pmed.R + Rd (31/31 gauge tests), closing the correction sweep.
   • Follow-up docs commit `4494d79` (2026-08-22, direct to dev, no PR — docs-only,
     existing files) — landed after PR #33 merged: dropped the "Lin et al. 2026"
     citation from oe_regular/weak_id docs (weak_id is a scale-only adaptation of
     Zhan's idea, not his statistic; Lin and Han's bootstrap-consistency result
     holds nuisances fixed and doesn't cover this package's refit-per-resample
     bootstrap), reframed se_method coverage as fold-split noise/SE instability
     rather than a biased formula (NEWS.md, R/gauge-pmed.R roxygen, both .Rd,
     vignettes/gauge-residual.qmd). Also added pkgdown reference sections for
     "Modern estimands" and "Sensitivity analysis" (_pkgdown.yml). Pushed to
     origin/dev.
